WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.302 --> 00:00:10.377
I had forgotten to close my curtain, so the full moon woke me. As I stretched out my arm toward the curtain, a scream split the night.

2
00:00:10.378 --> 00:00:19.877
What a cry! It came from the third floor, and my heart stood still as I heard a fierce struggle in the room above my own.

3
00:00:19.878 --> 00:00:32.112
"Help! Help!" a half-smothered voice called above me. "Rochester! Come!" the voice cried while the staggering and stamping went on wildly.

4
00:00:32.113 --> 00:00:37.119
A door opened on my floor, and then someone rushed along the corridor.

5
00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:44.777
Another foot stamped on the floor above, and something fell. At last there was silence.

6
00:00:44.778 --> 00:00:54.298
I threw on my robe, and though horror shook my limbs, went out into the darkened corridor, where all the guests were gathering and speaking at once.

7
00:00:54.299 --> 00:00:56.601
"Who's hurt?"

8
00:00:56.601 --> 00:00:58.535
"Are there robbers?"

9
00:00:58.536 --> 00:01:00.861
"Where's Mr. Rochester?"

10
00:01:00.862 --> 00:01:07.914
"Here I am!" Mr. Rochester descended the stairs from the third floor, carrying a candle.

11
00:01:07.915 --> 00:01:14.827
Blanche Ingram ran to him and seized his arm. "What awful event has taken place?"

12
00:01:14.828 --> 00:01:22.739
"A servant had a nightmare," he replied. "It's nothing. You must all return to your rooms now."

13
00:01:22.740 --> 00:01:35.983
I went back to my room, but I didn't sleep. Instead I dressed carefully and sat on the edge of my bed, waiting for I knew not what. At last someone tapped on my door.

14
00:01:35.984 --> 00:01:40.196
"Are you awake?" Mr. Rochester asked softly.

15
00:01:40.197 --> 00:01:43.897
I opened my door, and there he stood with a candle.

16
00:01:43.898 --> 00:01:48.319
"Do you have a sponge and some smelling salts?" he whispered.

17
00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:55.043
I nodded and fetched them from my room. He beckoned me to follow him upstairs.

18
00:01:55.043 --> 00:02:00.642
Outside a door he paused and said, "Do you turn sick at the sight of blood?"

19
00:02:00.643 --> 00:02:04.236
"I don't think so, but I haven't been tested."

20
00:02:04.237 --> 00:02:07.851
"Give me your hand because we can't risk a fainting fit."

21
00:02:07.852 --> 00:02:13.030
I put my fingers in his. "Warm and steady," he remarked.

22
00:02:13.030 --> 00:02:19.266
Inside the room a tapestry had been looped up on one side to reveal a door to another room beyond.

23
00:02:19.267 --> 00:02:23.867
I heard a snarling, dog-like sound coming from within.

24
00:02:23.868 --> 00:02:28.792
"Wait here," said Mr. Rochester as he went into the inner room.

25
00:02:28.793 --> 00:02:38.930
A shout of laughter greeted his entrance, followed by Grace Poole's goblin-like, "Ha-ha!" Then I heard a low voice address him.

26
00:02:38.931 --> 00:02:43.427
Soon Mr. Rochester came out and closed the door behind him.

27
00:02:43.428 --> 00:02:53.428
He directed me to the other side of some closed curtains, which concealed a large bed. A man sat in a chair next to the bed.

28
00:02:53.429 --> 00:03:00.413
His eyes were closed, but I recognized the pale and seemingly lifeless face of Mason.

29
00:03:00.414 --> 00:03:06.069
I saw too that one sleeve and one side of his shirt were almost soaked in blood.

30
00:03:06.070 --> 00:03:12.235
"Hold the candle," Mr. Rochester directed me as he began to sponge Mason's wounds.

31
00:03:12.236 --> 00:03:16.079
"Am I in immediate danger?" murmured Mason.

32
00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:22.309
"It's a mere scratch, Richard. I'll fetch a doctor for you, and you'll be on your way by morning."

33
00:03:22.310 --> 00:03:29.468
Mr. Rochester explained that he might be gone for an hour or two and that I was to sponge Mason's wounds.

34
00:03:29.469 --> 00:03:36.125
If the man felt faint, I was to put a glass of water to his lips and the smelling salts to his nose.

35
00:03:36.126 --> 00:03:45.548
"You're not to speak to each other," warned Mr. Rochester. "Do you understand? No conversation."

36
00:03:45.549 --> 00:03:50.854
And so he left the room and locked the door, and I was alone with Mason.

37
00:03:50.855 --> 00:03:55.613
How had this quiet stranger become involved in this web of horror?

38
00:03:55.614 --> 00:04:01.279
Why was he up here when I'd clearly heard Mr. Rochester assign him a room below?

39
00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:09.320
The night seemed to last forever. Sometimes I feared that Mason was dying, and I wasn't even allowed to speak to him!

40
00:04:09.321 --> 00:04:15.428
At last I heard Pilot barking outside, and Mr. Rochester returned with the doctor.

41
00:04:15.429 --> 00:04:19.502
"Now, good fellow, how are you?" asked Dr. Carter.

42
00:04:19.503 --> 00:04:23.589
"She tried to kill me," Mason replied weakly.

43
00:04:23.590 --> 00:04:31.423
"What's this?" said Dr. Carter, examining the wound in Mason's shoulder. "This wasn't done with a knife."

44
00:04:31.423 --> 00:04:40.152
"She bit me when Rochester got the knife away from her. It was frightful." Mason shuddered.

45
00:04:40.153 --> 00:04:45.246
"I told you to be on your guard when you went near her," said Mr. Rochester.

46
00:04:45.247 --> 00:04:54.406
"You should have waited until tomorrow and had me with you. Hurry, Carter. The sun will soon rise, and I must get him away from here."

47
00:04:54.407 --> 00:05:00.222
Mr. Rochester ordered me to go downstairs and fetch a clean shirt and Mason's cloak.

48
00:05:00.223 --> 00:05:09.636
Then, with the assistance of Dr. Carter, Mason walked downstairs and out to a waiting coach. Dr. Carter climbed in after him.

49
00:05:09.637 --> 00:05:13.705
Mason looked out the window and addressed Mr. Rochester.

50
00:05:13.706 --> 00:05:23.642
"Let her be taken care of. Let her be treated tenderly. Let her . . ." He stopped, overcome by tears.

51
00:05:23.643 --> 00:05:34.543
"I do my best," said Mr. Rochester. As the coach rolled away, he added, "I wish there were an end to this! Come walk with me, Jane."

52
00:05:34.544 --> 00:05:41.106
In the garden he gathered a rose, the first of the season, and offered it to me.

53
00:05:41.107 --> 00:05:47.914
"Thank you, sir," I said. Then I asked, "Will Grace Poole still live here?"

54
00:05:47.915 --> 00:05:52.277
"Oh yes! Now put her out of your thoughts."

55
00:05:52.278 --> 00:05:58.451
But I had more questions. "Is the danger that you feared last night gone now?"

56
00:05:58.451 --> 00:06:03.584
"I cannot vouch for that until Mason is out of England, and not even then.

57
00:06:03.585 --> 00:06:09.740
He wouldn't knowingly hurt me, but with one careless word he might deprive me of happiness."

58
00:06:09.741 --> 00:06:20.574
We came to an arbor, and he urged me to sit next to him. "Suppose that long ago a man committed not a crime, but an error.

59
00:06:20.575 --> 00:06:30.136
Now he meets someone whose good and bright qualities he has sought for twenty years. Would it be all right for him to attach himself to her?"

60
00:06:30.137 --> 00:06:34.168
He looked eagerly at me, but I didn't know how to answer him.

61
00:06:34.169 --> 00:06:40.550
While around us the birds were singing and the leaves rustling, I stayed silent.

62
00:06:40.551 --> 00:06:50.765
Then abruptly his tone changed. "You've noticed my tender feelings toward Miss Ingram. Do you think she'd regenerate me if I married her?"

63
00:06:50.766 --> 00:06:52.708
I didn't respond.

64
00:06:52.709 --> 00:06:59.287
"Jane, you're quite pale from the night's excitement. Are you angry that I disturbed your sleep?"

65
00:06:59.288 --> 00:07:00.798
"No, sir."

66
00:07:00.799 --> 00:07:07.120
"Then perhaps you'll sit up with me the night before I'm married because I know I won't be able to sleep."

67
00:07:07.121 --> 00:07:12.959
"Yes, sir," I answered. "I'd like to be useful whenever I can."

68
00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:19.610
"Oh, look! Two of our guests are at the stables. Go quickly so they don't see you."

69
00:07:19.611 --> 00:07:30.938
As I went one way and he went another, I heard him saying cheerfully to the men, "Mason was up before you all today. I rose at four to see him off."

